# T33234 — Port — Auto MDI/MDI-X — tb470 IE520 stack — 2026-09-29 — FAIL (script defect + one real finding)

Verdict: FAIL. Two cases ran, both FAILED, then the run was stopped (SIGINT 08:57:46) because
the framework PDU power-cycles the WHOLE bench (stk_a = 3 units, swi_b, swi_e, swi_f) after every
failed case ("Setup is no longer reliable - all devices will be rebooted"; 08:52:21 and 08:57:18)
and every remaining case would have failed the same way.
- TestCase_1 FAIL — script defect: the port-defaulting step sends `no polarity`, which is
  `% Invalid input` on BOTH the IE520 DUT and the x230 partner (the negation is `polarity auto`);
  the case grades any refused defaulting command as a STEP-1 FAIL. Nothing measured.
- TestCase_2 FAIL — REAL FINDING (measured, product-side or display): with the link UP
  (a-full a-1000) the IE520 reports `current polarity auto` on its copper-SFP test port
  port1.0.9 — no resolved mdi/mdix role — while the x230's fixed copper ports report mdi/mdix.
  The IE520-28GSX has no fixed copper port, so every copper case of this script depends on a
  resolved role the platform does not expose on a pluggable copper PHY. Whether that is a
  platform limitation, a defect, or a display gap is Terrence's call.
- TestCase_3..18 not run. 17–18 would be UNSUPPORTED (no fibre SFP cabled to a partner).
Run labelled: confounded — because of the `no polarity` defect (case 1) and the reboot-on-fail
behaviour; the case-2 reading itself is clean (same reading seen by hand at 08:39 and 08:42
before the run, on port1.0.2 and port1.0.9).

Operator: bench-runner subagent (device-testing-61 = sentinel, /test-mode shape A). Terrence
was at the bench with the crossover cable; no swap was ever requested.

