The defect: library_9001.py configureDefaultPort() sends `no speed`, `no duplex`, `no polarity`,
`no shutdown` (the docstring calls `no polarity` "the documented negation"); TestSet.configure()
and tear_down() in test-9001.33234.py send `no polarity` too. On awplus_main-20260923-20 (IE520)
and awplus 5.5.5_2-20260918-7 (x230) the negation is `polarity auto`. Note `no speed` and
`no duplex` were accepted (no refusal logged for them).
Fix (Test-cases): replace `no polarity` with `polarity auto` in all three places; then re-run.
Bench-side consequence: 2 × full-bench PDU power cycle (6 units), ~3.5 min to "all ports running"
each. The framework does this after EVERY failed TestCase in this run — a re-run of an 18-case
script with a platform-wide FAIL (case 2's reading) would power-cycle the bench up to 18 times.
Worth deciding before the re-run (queue I-3).

